# repos-manager

> A single CLI tool to clone and sync all your Git repositories from GitHub, GitLab, Forgejo, Bitbucket, and Radicle.

## What it does
repos-manager syncs Git repositories from multiple providers into a local directory structure that mirrors the remote namespace: host/owner/repo. It is a single native binary (written in Rust) for Linux, macOS and Windows.

## Key features
- Multi-provider: GitHub, GitLab, Forgejo/Gitea, Bitbucket, Radicle
- Parallel sync with configurable job count
- Status overview: dirty, ahead, behind, diverged repos
- Filter and ignore patterns
- Self-update with checksum verification
- Config file support
- Shell completions (bash, zsh, fish, PowerShell, elvish)

## Install
Linux / macOS: curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dxsk/repos-manager/main/installers/install.sh | sh
Windows (PowerShell): irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dxsk/repos-manager/main/installers/install.ps1 | iex
From source: cargo install --git https://github.com/Dxsk/repos-manager.git
Runtime requirements: git, plus the CLI of each provider (gh, glab, tea, bitbucket, rad)

## Usage
repos-manager login
repos-manager sync --all
repos-manager status

